      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have prepared a revised proposal that takes into account how the design appears to others and how it would be implemented if a scrollbar were included.\n\nAlthough not shown in the image below, it might also be worth considering standardizing the aspect ratios of the images displayed in the \"Social\" section and on the profile page.\n\nTo summarize my overall opinion: we should avoid unnecessary whitespace that does not improve readability, and instead provide a space for large, nearly square images designed to showcase content—rather than using thin, purely decorative images.\n\nOne might argue that the empty space is intended for future features, but in that case, I believe the current UI should have been released as the official version only once those features were actually ready.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-08-13T12:22:05.036Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "There is currently a significant disconnect between the intended visual presentation and the actual layout used to display these elements. If we truly value the role of profile and icon images, I believe we should adopt a more effective layout, such as the one described below.\n\nIt is best to use images based on the 4:3 aspect ratio used whenever possible.",
